@page "/help"
@inject TrueNasEndpointOptions TrueNasEndpoint

<PageTitle>Setup help · TrueNAS Update Manager</PageTitle>

<div class="page help-page">
    <header class="page-header">
        <div>
            <h1>Setup help</h1>
            <p class="subtitle">Create the TrueNAS account, connect securely, and finish the first-launch wizard.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="actions">
            <a class="button primary" href="/onboarding">Open setup wizard</a>
        </div>
    </header>

    <div class="notice" role="note">
        <strong>Connection rule:</strong> Continue stays disabled until Test connection succeeds. Use the API key owner's exact username and a key with <code>APPS_READ</code> and <code>APPS_WRITE</code>.
    </div>

    <nav class="panel help-toc" aria-label="Setup topics">
        <a href="/help#account"><span class="help-toc-number">1</span><span><strong>Account and key</strong><small>Create least-privilege access</small></span></a>
        <a href="/help#first-connection"><span class="help-toc-number">2</span><span><strong>Connect</strong><small>Enter and test the fields</small></span></a>
        <a href="/help#wizard"><span class="help-toc-number">3</span><span><strong>Finish setup</strong><small>Schedule, notify, discover</small></span></a>
        <a href="/help#troubleshooting"><span class="help-toc-number">4</span><span><strong>Troubleshoot</strong><small>Fix common first-run issues</small></span></a>
    </nav>

    <section id="account" class="panel help-section">
        <div class="help-heading">
            <span class="help-step-number" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
            <div>
                <h2>Create a service account and API key</h2>
                <p class="muted">Use a dedicated account instead of a personal administrator key.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <ol class="help-list">
            <li>In TrueNAS, open <strong>Credentials → Users</strong>, click <strong>Add</strong>, and create a user such as <code>autoupdate</code>. Keep Shell and SSH access disabled.</li>
            <li>Note the user's primary group. Open <strong>Credentials → Groups → Privileges</strong> and click <strong>Add</strong>.</li>
            <li>Select the service account's group under <strong>Local Groups</strong>. Add only <code>APPS_READ</code> and <code>APPS_WRITE</code>, leave Web Shell Access disabled, and save.</li>
            <li>Return to <strong>Credentials → Users</strong>, select the service account, and choose <strong>Add API Key</strong>. Copy the generated key immediately.</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="notice warning help-inline-notice">
            Treat the API key like a password. TrueNAS shows the complete value only when it is created or reset.
        </div>
    </section>

    <section id="first-connection" class="panel help-section">
        <div class="help-heading">
            <span class="help-step-number" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
            <div>
                <h2>Connect to TrueNAS</h2>
                <p class="muted">The secure endpoint is configured in the TrueNAS app deployment. Enter these values in Step 1 of the wizard.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <h3>Complete TrueNAS app YAML</h3>
        <p>Replace the entire custom app configuration with this YAML. It uses the current TrueNAS Web UI address, <code>10.0.0.21</code>.</p>
        <pre class="help-yaml"><code>services:
  truenas-update-manager:
    cap_drop:
      - ALL
    environment:
      ASPNETCORE_HTTP_PORTS: 2600
      DATA_PATH: /data
      TRUENAS_WEBSOCKET_URL: wss://truenas.local/api/current
    extra_hosts:
      - truenas.local:10.0.0.21
    image: ghcr.io/amitai5/truenasautoupdater:latest
    network_mode: host
    pull_policy: always
    read_only: true
    restart: unless-stopped
    security_opt:
      - no-new-privileges:true
    tmpfs:
      - /tmp:size=64m,mode=1777
    volumes:
      - update-manager-data:/data
volumes:
  update-manager-data: null
x-app-port: 2600</code></pre>

        <div class="table-wrap help-table">
            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>Field</th><th>Value</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Username</td><td>The API key owner's exact, case-sensitive username</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>API key</td><td>The value copied when the key was created</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Configured endpoint</td><td><code>@TrueNasEndpoint.ServerUrl</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Verify TLS certificate</td><td>Keep enabled when the certificate is trusted and covers <code>@TrueNasEndpoint.ServerUri.Host</code></td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>

        <p>Click <strong>Test connection</strong>. A successful test enables <strong>Continue</strong>. The app uses the validated <code>TRUENAS_WEBSOCKET_URL</code> from the deployment and does not expose the server address as an editable browser field.</p>

        <p class="muted">Prefer a stable hostname and a trusted certificate that covers it. When container DNS cannot resolve a local hostname, map that hostname to the TrueNAS IPv4 address with <code>extra_hosts</code> in the app YAML.</p>

        <div class="notice help-inline-notice">
            <strong>Need deeper diagnostics?</strong> A failed connection test displays an error code and diagnostic ID. Search the TrueNAS app's container logs for that ID to see the failing connection stage, DNS results, port, TLS setting, WebSocket error, and RPC method. Credentials and RPC payloads are never written to the log.
        </div>
    </section>

    <section id="wizard" class="panel help-section">
        <div class="help-heading">
            <span class="help-step-number" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
            <div>
                <h2>Finish the wizard</h2>
                <p class="muted">Nothing updates automatically until you explicitly assign policies.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="help-card-grid">
            <article>
                <h3>Schedule</h3>
                <p>Optionally enable scheduled checks. Use a five-field cron expression and an IANA timezone, for example <code>0 4 * * *</code> with <code>America/Los_Angeles</code>.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
                <h3>Notifications</h3>
                <p>Optionally configure SMTP email or an HTTPS webhook. Select only the event types you want and use each provider's test button.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
                <h3>Discovery</h3>
                <p>Discovery is read-only. Every app begins as <strong>Unconfigured</strong> and cannot auto-update until you review its policy.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section id="troubleshooting" class="panel help-section">
        <div class="help-heading">
            <span class="help-step-number" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
            <div>
                <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
                <p class="muted">Start with the symptom you see.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="help-troubleshooting">
            <details open>
                <summary>Test connection or Continue does nothing</summary>
                <p>Hard-refresh with <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>R</kbd>, confirm the newest container image is deployed, and verify <code>/_framework/blazor.web.js</code> returns HTTP 200 in browser developer tools. The page can look complete even when the Blazor handlers did not load.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Continue is disabled</summary>
                <p>This is expected until Test connection succeeds. Correct the connection, authentication, certificate, or role error shown above the form.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>TrueNAS keeps using an older image</summary>
                <p>Add <code>pull_policy: always</code> below the custom app's <code>image:</code> line, enable <strong>Apps → Configuration → Settings → Check for docker image updates</strong>, and save/redeploy the app. The pull policy checks GHCR when TrueNAS reapplies the app; it does not restart a running container by itself.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Authentication failed</summary>
                <p>Confirm the username owns the key, reset the key if its value is uncertain, and check whether an earlier insecure connection caused TrueNAS to revoke it.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Missing app permissions</summary>
                <p>Verify the service account's group is attached to a custom privilege containing both <code>APPS_READ</code> and <code>APPS_WRITE</code>. Do not edit built-in TrueNAS privileges.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>Certificate validation error</summary>
                <p>Confirm the certificate covers <code>@TrueNasEndpoint.ServerUri.Host</code>. Prefer correcting the hostname or certificate; otherwise disable certificate verification only on a trusted network.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>DNS failure, network unreachable, or connection refused</summary>
                <p>Verify <code>TRUENAS_WEBSOCKET_URL</code> and the <code>extra_hosts</code> mapping in the TrueNAS app YAML, then redeploy. The hostname should map to the current TrueNAS Web UI IPv4 address and the URL must end in <code>/api/current</code>.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
                <summary>No apps are discovered</summary>
                <p>Confirm the TrueNAS Apps service is running, at least one app is installed, and the service account has <code>APPS_READ</code>.</p>
            </details>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="panel help-section">
        <h2>More help</h2>
        <p>The repository's full setup guide includes installation, backups, security checks, and additional troubleshooting.</p>
        <div class="actions">
            <a class="button" href="https://github.com/Amitai5/TrueNASAutoUpdater/blob/production/docs/SETUP.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open full setup guide ↗</a>
            <a class="button" href="https://www.truenas.com/docs/scale/api/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TrueNAS API key guidance ↗</a>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
